-- busted configuration.
--
-- Without a ROOT, `busted` with no arguments exits 1 with "No test files
-- found matching Lua pattern: _spec", which makes the unit-test step
-- unusable in a gate (T-040).
--
-- The interpreter matters more than the paths. The game runs LuaJIT 2.0.2
-- (Lua 5.1). busted's launcher on this machine used to be PUC Lua 5.4, so
-- ToME-dialect code (loadstring, setfenv, unpack) failed under test while
-- being correct in-game, and 5.4-only syntax passed here and crashed there
-- -- the risk exactly backwards from how four documents described it.
--
-- Two guards, because either alone can be defeated (T-045):
--   * `lua = "luajit"` re-execs the suite under LuaJIT from PATH, so a
--     5.4 launcher cannot quietly run the tests in the wrong dialect. It
--     is a name, not a path, so it carries no machine's layout.
--   * spec/dialect_spec.lua asserts the dialect from inside a running
--     spec, which is the only check that cannot be bypassed by however
--     busted was invoked.
return {
  _all = {
    ROOT    = { "spec" },
    pattern = "_spec",
    lua     = "luajit",
  },
  default = {
    verbose = true,
  },
}
